content.text:
All three gates re-confirmed clean after the addendum:

- **`npx tsc --noEmit`** — clean (no output).
- **`npm run test`** — `Test Files 55 passed (55)`, `Tests 899 passed (899)`, including `zimmProductCard/index.test.tsx (73 tests)`.
- **`npm run lint`** — `26 problems (5 errors, 21 warnings)`, identical to the baseline established earlier in this session, zero new problems, none in `zimmProductCard/*`.

## Diff of this addendum

**`overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.tsx`** — the `!config.showContent` render branch now overrides `alt` on the two image copies passed to `ZimmProductCardMedia`:

```tsx
        <MediaOnlyCardLink to={href} display="block">
          <VisuallyHidden>{name}</VisuallyHidden>
          <ZimmProductCardMedia
            // alt overridden to '' on these two copies only — never on the shared
            // ZimmProductCardMediaImage type, never in the showContent branch above. The
            // VisuallyHidden name immediately above already supplies this link's accessible name;
            // without this override the image's own real alt text would be concatenated onto it
            // too (standard name-from-content computation for a link containing an <img>),
            // producing a redundant, doubled-up announcement instead of just the product name.
            // alt="" is the standard WCAG technique for exactly this case — a decorative-in-context
            // image inside an already-labelled link.
            primaryImage={{ ...primaryImage, alt: '' }}
            hoverImage={hoverImage ? { ...hoverImage, alt: '' } : undefined}
            images={images}
            swapOnHover={config.showHoverImageSwap && Boolean(hoverImage)}
            showControls
            badge={resolvedBadge}
          />
        </MediaOnlyCardLink>
```

The `ZimmProductCardMediaImage` type, the `true` branch (home/plp/wishlist), and `ZimmProductCardMedia`/`ZimmProductCardContent` themselves are untouched. `images` (the gallery array prop) is deliberately left unmodified — the coordinator's instruction named only `primaryImage`/`hoverImage`, and this variation's own design intent (AC 3, single index image only) means `images` is not expected to be populated here in practice; flagging this rather than silently expanding the instruction's scope.

Also updated in `index.tsx`: the module docblock's `recentlyViewed` paragraph now reads "The composed image's own `alt` is overridden to `''` on the copies of `primaryImage`/`hoverImage` passed into `ZimmProductCardMedia` here... `alt=''` is the standard WCAG technique... so the anchor's accessible name is exactly the product name" — replacing the prior "Left as-is: pass through unmodified" text.

**`index.test.tsx`** — the dedicated link test now asserts an exact match instead of a leading-substring one:

```tsx
  test('renders exactly one real, keyboard-reachable link, whose accessible name is exactly the product name', () => {
    wrap(<ZimmProductCard {...buildCardProps('recentlyViewed')} />);
    const links = screen.getAllByRole('link');
    expect(links).toHaveLength(1);
    expect(screen.getByRole('link', { name: 'Natura Dress' })).toHaveAttribute('href', '/product/1');
  });
```

(Docblock above it rewritten from "FLAGGED FOR RATIFICATION" to "RESOLVED (ratified by Marcel)", recording what was discovered and what fixed it.)

**`index.stories.tsx`** — the `RecentlyViewed` story's docblock updated: "Its accessible name is exactly the product name — the composed image's own `alt` is deliberately overridden to `''`... so it is not concatenated onto the link's accessible name" (replacing the "LEADS WITH the product name but is not only the product name" text).

## Confirmation

`git status --porcelain` still shows only the same three files modified, nothing staged:

